WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.028
Hi, I'm Abhishek, and this is Funnel of
Thought — built for the Agents of SigNoz

2
00:00:05.028 --> 00:00:07.028
hackathon.

3
00:00:07.028 --> 00:00:11.854
The idea: AI agents have a reasoning
contract — mine is plan, tool, validate,

4
00:00:11.854 --> 00:00:15.538
respond — and nothing today measures
whether they honour it.

5
00:00:15.538 --> 00:00:19.490
So I built three things: an
OpenTelemetry-instrumented LangGraph

6
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:24.182
agent; fot, a CLI that turns SigNoz Trace
Funnels into funnels-as-code over

7
00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:29.008
reasoning steps; and signoz-funnel-mcp —
the funnel tools SigNoz's MCP server

8
00:00:29.008 --> 00:00:31.008
doesn't ship.

9
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:34.759
All of it runs on self-hosted SigNoz,
installed with Foundry.

10
00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:39.837
My agent has a validation step. A
dashboard told me it ran in one hundred

11
00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:45.349
percent of runs. A funnel over the same
one hundred and twenty-five traces said

12
00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:47.349
sixty-four percent.

13
00:00:47.349 --> 00:00:52.138
Same traces. Both queries correct. Only
one asked the right question.

14
00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:57.300
Here's the funnel, live, over the agent's
reasoning. One twenty-five runs start. One

15
00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.300
twenty-five reach the tool call.

16
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.730
Then the cliff: only eighty reach
validate, in order. Sixty-four percent.

17
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.759
And the counts are printed on every bar —
a percentage without a denominator isn't

18
00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:10.759
evidence.

19
00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:15.481
This isn't my tool marking its own
homework — here's the same funnel inside

20
00:01:15.481 --> 00:01:20.267
SigNoz itself. Sixty-four percent. One
twenty-five, one twenty-five, eighty,

21
00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.163
eighty. Down thirty-six percent on step
three.

22
00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:28.138
Trace Funnels are a SigNoz primitive. No
other observability backend ships one.

23
00:01:28.138 --> 00:01:30.654
So why did the counter say one hundred?

24
00:01:30.654 --> 00:01:36.068
A counter only asks: did the span exist. A
funnel asks: did it happen after the

25
00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:38.068
previous step.

26
00:01:38.068 --> 00:01:43.553
Forty-five runs emitted their validate
span before the tool result existed — the

27
00:01:43.553 --> 00:01:46.866
agent validated an answer that hadn't
arrived yet.

28
00:01:46.866 --> 00:01:52.207
A counter measures presence. A funnel
measures sequence. Ordering lives in the

29
00:01:52.207 --> 00:01:54.207
trace, not the span.

30
00:01:54.207 --> 00:01:59.451
Here's one of those runs. Plan — then
validate, in red — and only then the tool

31
00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.451
call.

32
00:02:01.451 --> 00:02:05.793
It finished validating before the thing it
was validating existed.

33
00:02:05.793 --> 00:02:11.424
None of SigNoz's forty-one MCP tools reach
funnels, so I shipped the missing ones.

34
00:02:11.424 --> 00:02:16.712
Here, the agent calls get-funnel-analytics
and reads its own conversion rate.

35
00:02:16.712 --> 00:02:21.931
The read path has no model in it — it's
sub-second, deterministic, and free.

36
00:02:21.931 --> 00:02:26.927
What did I learn? Funnels need strictly
increasing timestamps. Two correct specs

37
00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:31.517
can be silently incompatible — that
finding is now two SigNoz issues and a

38
00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:36.038
pull request. And agents fail politely: no
errors, just skipped homework.

39
00:02:36.038 --> 00:02:41.034
So: watch validate-step conversion, and
alert on the cliff. Mine is firing right

40
00:02:41.034 --> 00:02:43.034
now.
